Summary of significant changes in this fork
--------------------------------------------
- Reworked the C++ plugin bridge: RAII socket handling, Content-Length-aware
  request reading with receive timeouts, loopback-only bind, and DNS-rebinding /
  cross-origin (Host/Origin) request rejection.
- Structured-exception hardening: request handlers translate Windows SEH faults
  into catchable C++ exceptions (/EHa + _set_se_translator) so a bad pointer
  returns HTTP 500 instead of crashing x64dbg.
- A substantially expanded, higher-level MCP toolset: launch/attach lifecycle,
  smart "run until" flows, console and GUI/UI-Automation automation, anti-debug
  and packer triage, OEP hunting, Scylla dump/fix, tracing (API/heap/instruction/
  coverage), snapshots, thread control, conditional tracing, symbol loading, and
  patched-binary export.
- Session binding, bridge self-check / drift detection, and smoke-test harnesses.

